abstract: >-
  This module teaches social scientists how to find, evaluate and collect
  geospatial data: searching data repositories, downloading U.S. Census Bureau
  boundaries and statistics with the Census API, acquiring scanned maps and
  satellite imagery, and collecting field data with QField, ending with a
  network analysis of grocery store access in QGIS.
